    "name": "Pacing Practice",
    "text": "2\nPacing Practice\n1 SECTION\nInstructions\n\nChoose an interval time goal.\n\nYour interval time goal is your target time for each question.\n\nFor example, an interval time goal may be 90 seconds per question.\n\nFollow the procedures of How to Set a Realistic Interval Time Goal below.\n\nSet an interval timer to repeatedly countdown from that time goal 30 times in a row.\n\nDo not incorporate rest intervals.\n\nWe choose 30 times so we can have some extra intervals in case our timer messes up.\n\nStart your interval timer when you begin an LR or RC section*.\n\nFor RC, only use the interval timer on the questions, not during the passage.\n\nYou must select an answer on each question before the interval timer goes off.\n\nYou cannot stay on a question longer than the interval timer permits, no matter how badly you want to.\nSEE FULL WORKOUT DETAILS",
